 "quality": {
  "flags": [
   "shared_cells_with_other_dataset"
  ],
  "notes": "Six second-life NMC cells cycled with residential and commercial duty cycles at Stanford. Cell ids G1, V4, V5 also appear in dataset_25. Cell spec is from LG's INR21700 M50 18.2Wh document (2017-09-22), the closest available datasheet to the exact M50T tab variant this dataset names; electrical/physical specs are expected to match across M50-series tab variants. Charge/discharge rate estimates, where explicitly marked raw_data in the citations, use signed observed current extrema divided by the stored nominal Ah. These are measurement estimates over the cached extraction scope, not imposed CC protocol setpoints; they may include pulse, dynamic, regenerative or diagnostic segments and measurement excursions. Current units and direction were checked against the cited original headers, status labels or separate charge/discharge counters. cached extraction covers six cells and parsed cycling, RPT and EIS workbook parts; the positive maximum includes diagnostic RPT charge rather than the grid-storage cycling protocol alone. stored nominal capacity 5.0 Ah comes from the nearest LG M50 datasheet, with an existing exact M50T model caveat; the inspected cycling workbook Global_Info Capacity field is 4.85. No denominator is inferred from measured current. Finite auxiliary temperature readings exist, but the sensor placement on the cell versus ambient air was not established; measured cell-temperature availability is therefore unclear."
 },
